	(text "JFOX TMR carrier.\\nThree PX4FMUv2.4.5 modules stacked on M3 + Richco R908-5 (7.95mm) spacers,\\ncabled to this board through their existing DF13 connectors.\\nMounting pattern is 30.0 x 30.0 mm, taken from the module's own .brd file."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "107a6efb-f9cf-4c08-9cc7-d6cbff50af72")
	)
	(text "CAN1 BUS - daisy chain, NOT a star. Keep every stub short.\\nNO TERMINATION ON THIS BOARD. Each module carries R409, a fixed 120R\\nacross CAN_H/CAN_L with no disable jumper (RC0402FR-07120RL, verified\\nfrom the FMU netlist). Three unmodified modules = 3x120R in parallel\\n= ~40R, a real signal-integrity fault.\\nREQUIRED: desolder R409 on the electrically-middle module only.\\nVerify ~60R across CAN_H/CAN_L with the bus unpowered before trusting it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "59efb58b-3e3c-4816-afd6-d1e60e8e9f72")
	)
	(text "POWER - three INDEPENDENT paths, one per module. Deliberately not commoned:\\nboard-level redundancy is meaningless if one supply can take all three down.\\nEach module still arbitrates its own inputs internally via LTC4417 (U1101).\\nBrick in -> module out; the only shared net here is GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "71fb4428-6eac-44de-83ef-c73c027bb3a3")
	)
